From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:44:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add threat-observability prototype (sensor, rules,
 enrichment, findings UI)

A request sensor turns /api/accounts/** calls into security events. Four
detection rules (BOLA, account enumeration, debit velocity, client-error
probing) are mapped to OWASP Top 10:2025 and MITRE ATT&CK, enriched with
threat intel and account value, scored, and deduplicated into persisted
findings. Adds /api/security/* endpoints, a Flyway migration, an Angular
Security page, sample vulnerability prioritisation (CVSS/EPSS/KEV/runtime
context), a demo traffic script and docs with an interview cheat sheet.

The sensor detects but does not fix the missing object-level authorisation
in the existing account endpoints; this is documented in the new docs.

